description:
Write the scene stack from lesson 2.05. Scenes are described by a name and whether they cover what is below them; requests made during an update are applied afterwards:

```cpp
struct Scene { std::string name; bool coversBelow; };

class SceneStack
{
public:
    void push(Scene s);       // requests: queued, applied by apply()
    void pop();
    void replace(Scene s);    // pop the top and push s (on an empty stack: just push)
    void clear();             // remove every scene
    void apply();             // carry out the queued requests in order, then forget them

    std::string top() const;                    // "" if empty
    std::vector<std::string> drawOrder() const; // bottom to top, starting at the highest covering scene
    std::size_t size() const;
};
```

- `pop` on an empty stack does nothing.
- `drawOrder` starts at the highest scene with `coversBelow == true` (or the bottom scene if none covers) and lists up to the top.

